<title>RUSSIA: SAS cancels Copenhagen-Minsk route.</title>
<headline>SAS cancels Copenhagen-Minsk route.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Scandinavian Airlines System (SAS) said on Monday its regular flights between Copenhagen and the Belarus capital, Minsk, would be cancelled from January, just four months after the service was opened.</p>
<p>SAS's Moscow office said in a statement the flights would be discontinued because the airline &quot;did not get the number of passengers it had anticipated for this destination&quot;.</p>
<p>Officials declined further comment.</p>
<p>SAS started the regular passenger flights in September. The company has been operating a 105-seater DC-9-41 three days a week on Mondays, Thursdays and Fridays.</p>
<p>--Viktor Anoshkin, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
